/** Generates `2 ** rounds` distinct strings that all share the same `Immutable.hash()`, by concatenating the classic "Aa"/"BB" collision blocks (both equal `65 * 31 + 97 === 66 * 31 + 66 === 2112` under the JVM-style `31 * h + c` string hash). Inserting these into a Map forces them all into a single HashCollisionNode — the hash-flooding scenario this code guards. */
